The file patches the real Go source of math/big/natconv.go.

go of the package math/big.

The real file guards the divisor cache of base 10 with a sync.Mutex. All Go
code runs in 1 Dart isolate, and a goroutine yields only at a point that
blocks. The critical section holds nat arithmetic alone, thus no other
goroutine reaches the cache while 1 goroutine builds it, and the lock never
finds the cache held.

The lock costs more than nothing. Mutex.Lock of the overlay waits on a channel,
thus stage 3 marks each caller of nat.itoa as a function that blocks. A
//gart:sync position then rejects each build method that formats a value of
this package. Once of the overlay drops its own lock for the same reason.

